6,7633,1188,20,13,23,11,17,13,24,29621,7,21,13,17,11,17,13,24,1106,1502,20912,47,3,44970,15,11,19,701,69214,317,1502,20912,50,3,44970,15,11,15,701,16844,317,1502,20912,49,3,44970,21,11,15,701,925,317,1502,20912,51,3,44970,21,11,17,701,36,317,1502,20912,48,3,44970,21,11,19,701,3944,317,24157,6405,60,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nIn the diagram, the area of rectangle $PQRS$ is $24.$ If $TQ = TR,$ what is the area of quadrilateral $PTRS?$ [asy]\nsize(100);\ndraw((0,0)--(6,0)--(6,4)--(0,4)--cycle);\ndraw((0,4)--(6,2));\ndraw((5.8,1.1)--(6.2,1.1));\ndraw((5.8,.9)--(6.2,.9));\ndraw((5.8,3.1)--(6.2,3.1));\ndraw((5.8,2.9)--(6.2,2.9));\nlabel(\"$P$\",(0,4),NW);\nlabel(\"$S$\",(0,0),SW);\nlabel(\"$R$\",(6,0),SE);\nlabel(\"$T$\",(6,2),E);\nlabel(\"$Q$\",(6,4),NE);\n[/asy]","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"8527fd0e991c3fca61b3c59f007735a5f92d41c0e732f7ca6fdad647e2c78e40"},"seconds":30.99303364753723,"seed":37356583791008047,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve this problem, we need to find the area of quadrilateral \\(PTRS\\) given that the area of rectangle \\(PQRS\\) is \\(24\\) and \\(TQ = TR\\). Let's break it down step by step.\n\n1. **Identify the coordinates of the points:**\n   Let's place the rectangle \\(PQRS\\) on the coordinate plane with \\(P\\) at \\((0, h)\\), \\(Q\\) at \\((w, h)\\), \\(R\\) at \\((w, 0)\\), and \\(S\\) at \\((0, 0)\\). Here, \\(w\\) and \\(h\\) are the width and height of the rectangle, respectively.\n\n2. **Calculate the area of the rectangle:**\n   The area of rectangle \\(PQRS\\) is given by:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Area} = w \\times h = 24\n   \\]\n\n3. **Determine the position of point \\(T\\):**\n   Since \\(TQ = TR\\) and \\(T\\) lies on the vertical line at \\(x = w\\), \\(T\\) must be the midpoint of \\(QR\\). Therefore, the coordinates of \\(T\\) are \\((w, \\frac{h}{2})\\).\n\n4. **Calculate the area of triangle \\(PQT\\):**\n   The base of triangle \\(PQT\\) is \\(w\\) (the width of the rectangle) and the height is \\(h - \\frac{h}{2} = \\frac{h}{2}\\). The area of triangle \\(PQT\\) is:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Area of } \\triangle PQT = \\frac{1}{2} \\times w \\times \\frac{h}{2} = \\frac{wh}{4} = \\frac{24}{4} = 6\n   \\]\n\n5. **Calculate the area of quadrilateral \\(PTRS\\):**\n   The area of quadrilateral \\(PTRS\\) is the area of the rectangle minus the area of triangle \\(PQT\\):\n   \\[\n   \\text{Area of } PTRS = \\text{Area of } PQRS - \\text{Area of } \\triangle PQT = 24 - 6 = 18\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the area of quadrilateral \\(PTRS\\) is \\(\\boxed{18}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{18}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
